A||||24||JSocha||What would you choose for 4"x10" speakers?||||5||
Z||000000||JSocha||09-27-2001||04:46 PM||||I'm going to be replacing my 87's 4x10's and taking the stock ones out and putting them in the 86GT for now as the 86 has not speakers in front.<P>If you had your choice, since they cost the same, which would you choose?<P><B>Kenwood's <u>KFC-415C</u></B><BR> <IMG SRC="http://pix.crutchfield.com/products/2000/113/l113KFC415C.jpeg">  for $99.95 <A HREF="http://www.crutchfield.com/cgi-bin/S-v3zbFEFB571/ProdView.asp?s=0&c=3&g=399&I=113KFC415C&o=&a=" TARGET=_blank>http://www.crutchfield.com/cgi-bin/S-v3zbFEFB571/ProdView.asp?s=0&c=3&g=399&I=113KFC415C&o=&a=</A> <P>or<P><B>Pioneer's <u>TS-A4103</u></B><BR> <IMG SRC="http://pix.crutchfield.com/products/2000/130/l130TSA4103.jpg">  for $99.95 <A HREF="http://www.crutchfield.com/S-v3zbFEFB571/cgi-bin/ProdView.asp?i=130TSA4103&s=0" TARGET=_blank>http://www.crutchfield.com/S-v3zbFEFB571/cgi-bin/ProdView.asp?i=130TSA4103&s=0</A> <P>Which sound better if you have experienced both as I would like the best quality to go with the stock radio, rear speakers and sub at this time?<P>I'm also going to be putting in a set of speaker baffles with the 4x10 speakers.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Master_Sushi||09-27-2001||05:39 PM||||I have the pioneers in my fiero. They sound good for a 4X10. I was powering them with a 200 watt pioneer amp. I could just barley get them to pop. I think they can handel allot of power and sound good doing it   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. <BR>I never heard the kenwood 4X10's but most people will tell you the pioneers are better. I honestly think most 4X10s will never sound that great. They are mostly for mid bass. To get deep bass out of a fiero you need a sub.<P>But any aftermarket speaker is better then OEM gm paper coned full ranges   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<P>------------------<BR>88 Fiero Coupe...<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mesopotamis_1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 09-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||09-27-2001||05:48 PM||||I'm curious on this topic. I've got that set of pioneers sitting in my garage staring at me every day.  I'm listening for opinions as well!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fullstaff.gif">   <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000003||Boomtastic||09-27-2001||06:07 PM||||Neither. If your heart's set on 4x10's, look for Pyle. Otherwise, switch to a component set. Of course, some enterprising indivuduals have squeezed 6x9's in the dash without modifications ...<P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000004||stimpy||09-27-2001||06:21 PM||||You can find Pyles pretty easily. Check Flea Markets and Swap Meets. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Personally I like the Pioneers, but the Kenwoods will give better and clearer highs. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||85ZainoGT||09-27-2001||08:44 PM||||from my experience, pioneers sound better... all around..||||reg||1
Z||000006||turbo86se||09-27-2001||09:53 PM||||I've always liked Pioneers, but for the SE I tried a set of Audiobahns. I love them. They were only $70, and sound incredible.<BR>Much better than the JVC's in the '88, IMHO.||||reg||1
Z||000007||RossT||09-27-2001||11:54 PM||||Jeff, I have the Kenwoods and am very happy!<BR>Some have said that the kenwood highs are better than the Pioneers, but the Pioneers lows are better than the Kenwoods.  I have the Sub system, so I am not to concerned about the lows.<P>Tell us about the 86, I must have missed the details!!!<P>The lambo has had alot of work don to it in the past month.  Fiberglass work is almost done.  Alignment is done and its up and running.<P>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000008||Hippocrat||09-28-2001||12:06 AM||||Really depends on what you want .. <P>Looks like pretty much everyone is in agreement. Kenwood will provide clearer highs and the Pioneers are a better mid. <P>If you like really crisp sound, I would go with the Kenwoods.<P>You mention you have the sub so that should provide the mid you need (not having heard the stock fiero subs I'm referring to it as mid Yes )<P>Preference makes the choice here I would say.||||reg||6
Z||000009||MikeSchaefer||09-28-2001||12:06 AM||||I have had two pairs of Pioneers, one pair Kenwoods, and a pair of Jensens, and I will vouge for what RossT said.  K's give better high, but P's give better lows & pop less.<BR>I guess it just depends on what other speakers you'll be having, if you have a sub get the Kenwoods, if not go with pioneers.  Don't get Jensens whatever you do.  From my experience Pyle is a low quality brand isn't it?<BR>Both Pioneer and Kenwood sound very good though, so it's win/win.<BR>Mike Schaefer<BR>http//surf.to/fiero||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroRyan||09-28-2001||01:55 AM||||My Soundstorm's are pretty good, nice sound quality...  but I'm going to be getting Pioneers when I get some free $$  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Boomtastic||09-28-2001||04:41 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>You can find Pyles pretty easily. Check Flea Markets and Swap Meets.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Personally I like the Pioneers, but the Kenwoods will give better and clearer highs. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That would be the same Pioneers & Kenwoods that you can buy in Wal*Mart, right?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Put either up against those Pyles and see which will outlast the other when put under severe duty. I've shredded Pioneers, and the Sonys? Let's just say that those are even weaker ..<P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Boomtastic||09-28-2001||04:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MikeSchaefer:<BR><B>From my experience Pyle is a low quality brand isn't it?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Pyle Driver = low quality? Uhhhhhhh, no. I lost respect for Pioneers when I could walk into any discount auto store and find them sitting on the shelf, right next to Kraco products ... 'nuff said?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||grinthock||09-28-2001||07:23 AM||||4x10?  Do'nt.... Just Do'nt...  I used Boston Acoustik Rally componants, use them and then make an adaptor plate, WAY easy, WAY better sound<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif"> </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000014||gangrenefiero||09-28-2001||08:44 AM||||I have 12 speakers in my car. I have the pioneer 4 X 10s in the front. They are way better than factory and if you want loudness you can put a 200 watt amp on it and they will be great. But there is plenty of room behind the seats for 10in subs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||gangrenefiero||09-28-2001||08:46 AM||||OH also if you check on ebay, there is  a lot of deals with speakers and componets. 4 x 10s brand new will run about 70, so you save some, or you could just buy it from the store, but its worth checking out.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Ditz88GT||09-28-2001||09:45 AM||||I have to think component sets are the best way to go, but I have a set of Kicker 4X10s which work great.<P><P>------------------<BR>~Ditz88GT<P>E-mail: cditzler@hotmail.com<BR>AIM: Ditz88GT<BR>http://go.to/fiero||||reg||3
Z||000017||Raydar||09-28-2001||12:21 PM||||I've got the Pioneers. They sound pretty good with a Delco CD player. They rattle a bit at high volume. Could be the grills or the installation, though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <BR>Sound waaayyyyy better than stock.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000018||Oreif||09-28-2001||12:36 PM||||Pioneers have a great mid-range and OK highs.<BR>Kenwoods have a great highs and an OK mid range.<BR>Both speakers have OK Bass.<BR>Pyles have excellent bass and highs but OK on mid-range.<BR>Alpine and Sony is average at all three levels.<BR>Your best bet is to go around and listen to what you prefer with the type of music.<BR>I didn't like the Pioneers because I like the highs crisper. <P>Pyle and Kenwood use hard dome tweeters and the others use soft dome tweeters.<BR>I am not sure who all is still making 4X10's<BR>they seem to be getting harder to find. The Alpine and Sony's I think are not made any more.||||reg||1
Z||000019||JSocha||09-28-2001||01:26 PM||||I just want a good sounding set for now to replace the stock 4x10 that will work with the stock "I'm a very cheap DELCO" radio.  <P>The speakers in my 87 that I'm replacing are going over into the 86 for now which is my daughters college car.<P>After I restore the interior and exterior of my 87, then I'm looking into a "kick-you-in-the-butt" car stereo system.  Two years down the road.  Hopefully going to install a DVD player at that time when they come down in price  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<P>Any recommendation for the MODEL to look at as far as PYLE's go?<P>I'm looking at the current buy now listings and prices on eBay as well as at mysimon.com||||reg||1
Z||000020||Rick 88||09-28-2001||01:33 PM||||My car has Alpines. I still have the stock EQ cassette and sub. The radio has enough power to drive them and they sound better than the original Delcos.||||reg||1
Z||000021||ds21||09-28-2001||05:01 PM||||I also would choose seperates over 4x10's, as they tend to be more accurate, but some people don't like accurate witch is ok too. I used to work at a very big audio/video store and all I can say is "you'll know what you like when you hear" it so trust you own ears! It's the same as T.V.s you get used to yours and soon everybody elses looks funny.<BR>Good luck!<P>P.S. make sure the sales person is not using an amp or e.q. as even a low powered "quality" amp can make a big diff. (unless you plan on getting one witch is always a good ideal)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by ds21 (edited 09-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||JSocha||09-28-2001||05:52 PM||||<FONT SIZE="3"><B>DOH!</B></FONT><P>LOL! I'm just glad I didn't ask which way the toilet paper should be hung/put on the dispenser...with the paper over the top or from behind and down.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> hehehehehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000023||Formula88||09-28-2001||09:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Boomtastic:<BR><B> Pyle Driver = low quality? Uhhhhhhh, no. I lost respect for Pioneers when I could walk into any discount auto store and find them sitting on the shelf, right next to Kraco products ... 'nuff said?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Um, I've seen Pyle Drivers for sale in convenience stores.  I rate them BELOW Kraco, or no better at best.||||reg||13
Z||000024||JSocha||09-28-2001||09:53 PM||||Its settled for now:<P>Tonight I bought a set of the KENWOOD KFC-415C for the '87GT ($75.00 + $8 some SH).<P>And then a set of PYLE PLS413 (3-ways)($49.99 + $15SH - Grand Total: $64.99) for the '86GT to fill the empty holes  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  I was going to get the 2-way's but it was only minor pocket change to go to the 3-way's (daughters pockets  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ).<P>I'll keep you posted what I think of both sets and the sound off of the stock radio's in a future post after they are installed.  <P>Next question, does one just pry up the speaker grills on the dash where they are located or do you have to remove the whole dash.  Never done this before on a Fiero.<P>Would like to know now instead of finding out later when it is too late and the grill and dash are damaged.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
